      "answer_markdown": "### Source-Verified Evidence (`MODEL_PROPOSED`, not expert-reviewed)\n\n1. **Plyometric Training Raises Countermovement Jump Height in Sprinters** (`PMC9000001`, passage `bad20803b9b2...`, anchor `jats:#p-0` chars `0..136`): \"In a randomized controlled trial of 36 sprinters, countermovement jump height increased by 14.2% (p < 0.001), measured at 48.5 ± 4.1 cm.\"\n   - Model paraphrase (NOT independently verified; rely on the quotation above): The sprinter study reported increased countermovement jump height after training.\n   - Checks: source quotation `VERIFIED` · numbers `NOT_APPLICABLE` · wording `SUPPORTED_BY_LEXICAL_HEURISTIC` (heuristic, not entailment) · expert review `NOT_REVIEWED`\n2. **Drop Jump Flight Time Is Unchanged by Plyometric Training in Runners** (`PMC9000002`, passage `c4aa20bc5a11...`, anchor `jats:#p-0` chars `0..135`): \"In a crossover study of 18 runners, drop jump flight time did not change (p = 0.41), measured in milliseconds (ms) using a contact mat.\"\n   - Model paraphrase (NOT independently verified; rely on the quotation above): The runner study reported no change in drop-jump flight time.\n   - Checks: source quotation `VERIFIED` · numbers `NOT_APPLICABLE` · wording `SUPPORTED_BY_LEXICAL_HEURISTIC` (heuristic, not entailment) · expert review `NOT_REVIEWED`\n\n> 1 proposed claim(s) were **rejected** and are not shown (`claim_not_supported_by_quoted_span`).\n\n#### Cross-Study Comparison (`INCOMPATIBLE_OUTCOMES_OR_UNITS`)\nThe studies share no outcome terms and no explicit measurement unit; numerical pooling or direct effect-size equivalence is not supported by the extracted evidence.\n\n---\n*All study findings, comparisons, and synthesized claims are MODEL_PROPOSED / PROPOSED. Exact quotation and canonical source-span checks verify text provenance only and do not establish scientific entailment, study validity, clinical applicability, or expert review.*",
